# Content directories — wholly untracked, structure included. They hold only
# per-user content: PDFs, LLM-authored pages, supplementary files, and the
# wiki/index.md + wiki/log.md bookkeeping that lives inside the Obsidian vault.
# `researchwiki init` creates them (see categories.DEFAULT_DIRS for the
# page-type scaffold); nothing here is committed, so there is no .gitkeep.
#
# Written WITHOUT a trailing slash on purpose. A trailing slash matches
# directories only, and these paths are frequently symlinks into a synced
# folder (see prompts/migration-backfill.md) — which git does not treat as a
# directory, so `/wiki/` would leave the symlink showing as untracked.
/papers
/inbox
/wiki
# Obsidian Web Clipper drops — per-user captured content, never part of the repo.
# No trailing slash, same reason as above: it may be a symlink into the vault.
/Clippings
# Everything this repo emits for someone else to look at, under one roof:
#   output/graph.html   `visualize`
#   output/okf/         `export --format okf`
#   output/share/       `prompts/share-page.md`
# All of it is per-user, regenerable from wiki/, and carries page titles from a
# private corpus — so the umbrella is ignored wholesale rather than per-artifact,
# and a new generator needs no .gitignore change to stay out of git.
output/

# Legacy location of output/share/, kept ignored so a stale directory on a second
# synced machine doesn't surface as untracked after the move.
share/

# Per-user "I dismissed the suggest-splits warning at this time" stamp.
# Touched by `researchwiki suggest-splits`; status uses it to suppress
# the `wiki/other/` saturation warning for the decay window.
.suggest-splits-stamp

# Companion stamp for the within-category divergence nudge (status uses it to
# suppress `suggest-splits --category` reminders for the decay window).
.category-divergence-stamp

# Companion stamp for the claim-overlap backlog nudge (status uses it to
# suppress `claim-overlap --backlog` reminders for the decay window).
.claim-overlap-stamp

# Per-user "I decided this isn't a concept" denylist for concept-hub
# candidates that failed the concept-vs-glossary thesis test. Written by
# `researchwiki candidates concepts --decline`; read by `collect_candidates`
# so a rejected term stops resurfacing. Curatorial state, not code — same
# bucket as `wiki/*` and the stamps above.
.concept-declines.json

# Companion stamp for the claim-pair discovery nudge (status uses it to
# suppress `candidates pairs` reminders for the decay window).
.claim-discovery-stamp

# Per-user "these two papers aren't related" denylist for the claim-pair
# discovery queue. Written by `candidates pairs --decline`; read by
# `discover_pairs` so a reviewed-and-rejected pair stops re-proposing.
# Curatorial state, same bucket as `.concept-declines.json` above.
.pair-dismissals.json

# Active LLM model config — per-user, mutable. Every `config/models.*.yaml`
# template IS tracked (chatgpt — the default, mirrored by the zero-config
# hardcoded fallback — plus anthropic, gemini*, glm, gemma, lmstudio,
# openai-compatible); `config/models.yaml` is the live copy a user selects by
# `cp config/models.chatgpt.yaml config/models.yaml` and then edits (provider
# swaps, per-role mixing). Prefer `RW_MODELS_CONFIG=models.<name>.yaml` to
# switch backends without copying at all.
# Gitignored so local A/B edits don't churn the repo or fight `git pull`.
config/models.yaml

# Ephemeral processing artifacts.
# No trailing slash: on a machine that keeps this repo inside a synced folder
# (iCloud/Dropbox), these are relocated outside it and symlinked back in, and a
# `dir/` pattern does NOT match a symlink — git would report every one as
# untracked. Bare names match both the real directory and the symlink.
.ingest
.s2-cache
.crossref-cache
.web-cache
.tantivy-index
.grade-cache
.semantic-cache
.claim-graph
.figures-cache
.mutation
.evolve-cache
.agent-output
.llm-relay
.benchmark-runs

# Pre-write snapshots taken by the maintainer-only repair passes in `internal/`
# before they rewrite wiki prose. `wiki/*` is gitignored, so a bad rewrite has
# no `git checkout` to undo it and these copies are the only recourse —
# timestamped per run, deleted once the result has been eyeballed.
.repair-backup-*

# Editor / vault configs (user-specific)
.obsidian/
.claude/
*.base

# OS / editor detritus
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/

# Per-user LLM backend credentials and routing config, including named profiles
# such as `.env.litellm`. Template: copy from config/models.*.yaml comments,
# fill in key + URL.
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
.acceptance/
.evaluate-output/
.eval-output/

# Local state DB. Canonical path is ~/.local/share/researchwiki/state.db;
# the package directory should never hold one — entry catches stray copies.
# `.researchwiki.db` covers another stray location (repo root) where some
# code paths drop a state DB.
researchwiki/db/state.db
.researchwiki.db

# Per-model retrieval caches built by the retrieval-fixture eval harness.
# Each candidate embedding (BGE-small, SPECTER2, etc.) gets its own
# `.retrieval-cache-{slug}/` with claim + page vectors. Local-only.
.retrieval-cache-*/
.eval-sandbox/

# WIP planning drafts and agent run logs — local only, must never be committed.
turboquant-single-cell-phase0-plan.md
.agent-runs/

# Internal maintainer-only artifacts (design notes, backfill/calibration
# helpers). Present in the working tree for the author's use; not shipped
# in the public repo.
internal/

# Local state DB — repo-root fallback path (some tools open it here
# before resolving the canonical ~/.local/share/researchwiki/state.db).
.state.db
